    {
      "id": "z2baQBVAY4h7dEzr1u8i2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1535.485950291658,
      "y": -198.16477326415858,
      "width": 671,
      "height": 1050,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 40,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0NV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 168011806,
      "version": 435,
      "versionNonce": 1429699678,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794649945811,
      "created": 1794648200109,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Http application data is encrypted using symmetric encryption\nalgo.-> AEAD means Authenticated Encryption with Associated\nData.\n\n-> Confidentiality: attackers cannot read the encrypted data.\n\n-> Integrity/authenticity: modifications to the ciphertext\nare detected.\n\nEX.\n-> AES-256-GCM\n-> ChaCha20-Poly1305\n\nWhy not use RSA?\n- Computationally expensive\n- Has size limitation for plain text.\n\nwhy not sha?\n- sha is not reversible\n\n\n           BROWSER                         SERVER\n              |                               |\n              |         ClientHello           |\n              |------------------------------>|\n              |                               |\n              |          ServerHello          |\n              |<------------------------------|\n              |                               |\n              |   ECDHE key exchange          |\n              |                               |\n              |  Both derive shared secret    |\n              |                               |\n              |       HKDF key derivation     |\n              |                               |\n              |   Client encryption key       |\n              |   Server encryption key       |\n              |                               |\n              |                               |\n              |===== AES-GCM encrypted =======|\n              |         HTTP data             |\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "uSGlh5UEZMSKhk-xbsjnw",
      "originalText": "Http application data is encrypted using symmetric encryption algo.-> AEAD means Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data.\n\n-> Confidentiality: attackers cannot read the encrypted data.\n\n-> Integrity/authenticity: modifications to the ciphertext are detected.\n\nEX.\n-> AES-256-GCM\n-> ChaCha20-Poly1305\n\nWhy not use RSA?\n- Computationally expensive\n- Has size limitation for plain text.\n\nwhy not sha?\n- sha is not reversible\n\n\n           BROWSER                         SERVER\n              |                               |\n              |         ClientHello           |\n              |------------------------------>|\n              |                               |\n              |          ServerHello          |\n              |<------------------------------|\n              |                               |\n              |   ECDHE key exchange          |\n              |                               |\n              |  Both derive shared secret    |\n              |                               |\n              |       HKDF key derivation     |\n              |                               |\n              |   Client encryption key       |\n              |   Server encryption key       |\n              |                               |\n              |                               |\n              |===== AES-GCM encrypted =======|\n              |         HTTP data             |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
