      "text": "Security Group vs mLTS \n\nSecurity Group: Is this network connection allowed?\n\nmTLS: Does the connecting service possess a trusted\nclient certificate?\n\nNACL — Network Access Control List\nA NACL is a stateless firewall applied at the\nsubnet level.",
      "fontSize": 24.946860136596786,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Security Group vs mLTS \n\nSecurity Group: Is this network connection allowed?\n\nmTLS: Does the connecting service possess a trusted client certificate?\n\nNACL — Network Access Control List\nA NACL is a stateless firewall applied at the subnet level.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
